NotoColorEmoji.ttf is Noto Color Emoji, from the Google Noto Fonts
project, licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.

    Source:  https://github.com/googlefonts/noto-emoji
    License: https://scripts.sil.org/OFL

It is compiled into the binary with include_bytes! and used only to
render the captcha images.

nsfw.onnx is Marqo/nsfw-image-detection-384, licensed under the
Apache License 2.0.

    Source:  https://huggingface.co/Marqo/nsfw-image-detection-384
    ONNX:    https://huggingface.co/ICIJ/nsfw-image-detection-384-onnx
    License: https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

It is compiled into the binary with include_bytes! and used only by the
NSFW lock, to score a thumbnail. It takes RGB [1, 3, 384, 384] scaled to
-1..1 (mean and standard deviation of 0.5) and emits two logits, in the
order nsfw, sfw.

nsfw_grade.onnx is mobilenetv4_conv_small.e2400_r224_in1k_nsfw_classifier,
licensed under the Apache License 2.0.

    Source:  https://huggingface.co/taufiqdp/mobilenetv4_conv_small.e2400_r224_in1k_nsfw_classifier
    License: https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

It is compiled into the binary with include_bytes! and used only by the
NSFW lock, to tell explicit content apart from merely revealing content.
It takes RGB [3, 224, 224] in 0..1 and applies its own ImageNet
normalisation; it emits five logits, in the order drawings, hentai,
neutral, porn, sexy.

libonnxruntime.so.1.20.1 is ONNX Runtime, licensed under the MIT License.

    Source:  https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime
    Release: https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime/releases/tag/v1.20.1
    License: https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime/blob/main/LICENSE

It is compiled into the binary with include_bytes! and written beside the
executable on first start, so that a deploy stays a single file. It runs
both models above; it replaced tract, which produced identical scores but
took twelve times as long per forward pass on the deployment hardware.

ocr_det.onnx and ocr_rec.onnx are the mobile detection and English
recognition models from PaddleOCR, licensed under the Apache License 2.0.

    Source:  https://github.com/PaddlePaddle/PaddleOCR
    ONNX:    https://huggingface.co/monkt/paddleocr-onnx
    License: https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

They are compiled into the binary with include_bytes! and used only by the
advertisement lock, to read text that was written into a picture. Detection
takes RGB [1, 3, h, w] with both sides a multiple of 32, ImageNet
normalised, and emits a probability map; recognition takes RGB
[1, 3, 48, w] scaled to -1..1 and emits per-step class logits decoded by
greedy CTC against ocr_dict.txt, which ships beside them and is part of the
same release.

clip.onnx is the vision tower of CLIP ViT-B/32, licensed under the MIT
License.

    Source:  https://github.com/openai/CLIP
    Weights: https://huggingface.co/openai/clip-vit-base-patch32
    ONNX:    https://huggingface.co/Xenova/clip-vit-base-patch32

It is the one model that is not part of this repository: at 335 MB it is
loaded from a file of that name beside the executable, because embedding it
makes rustc materialise the whole array into the object file and the link
needs several gigabytes. It is used only by the topic locks, to turn a
thumbnail into a 512-value embedding. It takes RGB
[1, 3, 224, 224] normalised with CLIP's own mean and standard deviation
and emits image_embeds directly. Only the vision tower ships; the text
tower was run once, offline, to produce the concept vectors in
src/handlers/concept_vectors.rs and is not part of this program.

